title: A new proposal for National Unity
subtitle: Can a unity list [? if jxsi_formed: be renewed? ?][? if not jxsi_formed: work this time? ?]
view-if: president_party != "cup" and cat_caretaker_gov and not jxcat_formed and jxcat_formation_trigger and (player_party == "cup" or player_party == "erc")
tags: event
new-page: true
max-visits: 1
role: event
on-arrival: {!
    {
        const CDC = ["ciu", "cdc", "dl", "pdcat", "junts"];
        const num = (value) => Number.isFinite(Number(value)) ? Number(value) : 0;
        const cdc = Q.parlament_current_ciu;
        Q.jxcat_cdc_leader = Q[cdc + "_leader"];
        Q.jxcat_cdc_relations = num(Q[cdc + "_relations"]);
        // Separate Parlament support is the current balance. A common list has
        // no individual polling: use its allocation only as a fallback, then
        // prefer existing results in contests the parties fought separately.
        let erc = 0, right = 0, cup = 0;
        const pooled = Q.erc_in_jxsi && !Q.jxsi_dissolved;
        const ercAllocation = num(Q.jxsi_formation_num || 50) / 100;
        for (const c of Q.parlament_constituencies || []) {
            for (const d of Q.parlament_demographics || []) {
                const suffix = `_parlament_${c}_${d}_support`;
                const pop = num(Q[`parlament_${c}_${d}_pop`]);
                if (pooled) {
                    const common = num(Q["jxsi" + suffix]) * pop;
                    const cupAllocation = Q.cup_in_jxsi
                        ? Math.min(100, Math.max(10, num(Q.jxsi_cup_formation_num))) / 100 : 0;
                    erc += common * (1 - cupAllocation) * ercAllocation;
                    right += common * (1 - cupAllocation) * (1 - ercAllocation);
                    cup += Q.cup_in_jxsi ? common * cupAllocation : num(Q["cup" + suffix]) * pop;
                }
                else {
                    erc += num(Q["erc" + suffix]) * pop;
                    right += num(Q[cdc + suffix]) * pop;
                    cup += num(Q["cup" + suffix]) * pop;
                }
            }
        }
        // CUP outside JxSi negotiates from current support against the common
        // ballot. CUP already inside retains its negotiated places, since
        // pooled support cannot tell us its separate current polling.
        Q.jxcat_cup_formation_num = Math.max(10,
            Math.round(erc + right + cup > 0 ? 100 * cup / (erc + right + cup) : 0));
        Q.jxcat_erc_balance = erc + right > 0 ? erc / (erc + right) : 0;
        Q.jxcat_left_balance = erc + right + cup > 0 ? (erc + cup) / (erc + right + cup) : 0;
        if (pooled) {
            let ercWeighted = 0, ercWeight = 0, leftWeighted = 0, leftWeight = 0;
            for (const [contest, suffix, importance] of [
                ["congreso", "_congreso_pv_cat", 0.4],
                ["local", "_local_barcelona_pv", 0.2],
                ["local", "_local_rb_pct", 0.2],
                ["local", "_local_interior_pct", 0.2],
            ]) {
                const ercUnited = ["jxsi", "jxcat"].some(list => Q[`erc_in_${list}`] && (Q[`${list}_in_${contest}`] ||
                    (contest === "local" && Q[`${list}_united_local`])));
                if (ercUnited)
                    continue;
                const e = num(Q["erc" + suffix]);
                // Old territorial holdings can survive a rename: never sum brands.
                const r = Math.max(...CDC.map(p => num(Q[p + suffix])));
                if (e + r <= 0)
                    continue;
                ercWeighted += importance * e / (e + r);
                ercWeight += importance;
                const cupUnited = ["jxsi", "jxcat"].some(list => Q[`cup_in_${list}`] && (Q[`${list}_in_${contest}`] ||
                    (contest === "local" && Q[`${list}_united_local`])));
                if (cupUnited)
                    continue;
                const u = num(Q["cup" + suffix]);
                leftWeighted += importance * (e + u) / (e + r + u);
                leftWeight += importance;
            }
            if (ercWeight)
                Q.jxcat_erc_balance = ercWeighted / ercWeight;
            if (leftWeight)
                Q.jxcat_left_balance = leftWeighted / leftWeight;
        }
        // Incumbency offers a free candidacy; it never excludes alternatives.
        // Affiliation establishes eligibility even if the party changed leaders.
        Q.jxcat_president_kind = "";
        if (Q.rubicon && Q.president && [cdc, "erc", "jxsi"].includes(Q.president_party)) {
            if (Q.president_party === "jxsi") {
                const party = [cdc, "erc"].find(p => Q[p + "_leader"] === Q.president);
                Q.jxcat_president_kind = party === cdc ? "cdc" : party ||
                    (Q.jxsi_formation_num < 50 ? "cdc" : Q.jxsi_formation_num > 50 ? "erc" : "neutral");
            } else {
                Q.jxcat_president_kind = Q.president_party === cdc ? "cdc" : Q.president_party;
            }
        }
        Q.jxcat_president_civic_veto = Q.player_party === "erc" && !!Q.jxcat_president_kind &&
            num(Q.erc_civic_strength) >= 30;
        Q.jxcat_president_available = !!Q.jxcat_president_kind && !Q.jxcat_president_civic_veto;
        Q.jxcat_select_president = false;
        Q.jxcat_civic_veto = Q.player_party === "erc" && num(Q.erc_civic_strength) >= 30;
        Q.jxcat_erc_repeat_veto = Q.player_party === "cup" &&
            !!Q.jxsi_formed && Q.jxsi_formation_num < 50 &&
            !(Q.jxcat_president_available && Q.president === Q[cdc + "_leader"]);
        Q.jxcat_failed_renewal = false;
        Q.jxcat_selected_leader = "";
        // The ANC puts forward one civic candidate. CUP can back Cuixart
        // without entering the list; its membership is a separate decision.
        const cupBacksCompromise = Q.player_party === "cup" ||
            (Q.cup_faction !== "Endavant" && num(Q.cup_relations) >= 55);
        Q.jxcat_neutral_candidate = num(Q.independence_movement) >= 85 &&
            Q.jxcat_left_balance >= 0.65 - 1e-9 && cupBacksCompromise
            ? "Jordi Cuixart" : "Jordi Sànchez";
        Q.jxcat_cdc_available = !Q.jxcat_erc_repeat_veto;
        Q.jxcat_neutral_available = num(Q.party_resources) >= 1 &&
            (Q.player_party === "erc"
                ? Q.jxcat_cdc_relations >= 55 && num(Q.erc_civic_strength) >= 15
                : Q.jxcat_cdc_relations >= 65 && num(Q.erc_relations) >= 65);
        Q.jxcat_erc_available = !Q.jxcat_civic_veto &&
            Q.jxcat_erc_balance >= 0.65 - 1e-9 && Q.jxcat_cdc_relations >= 65 &&
            num(Q.party_resources) >= 1;
        // Do not let the normal party option bypass a veto on the same person.
        if (Q.jxcat_president_civic_veto) {
            if (Q.president === Q[cdc + "_leader"]) Q.jxcat_cdc_available = false;
            if (Q.president === Q.erc_leader) Q.jxcat_erc_available = false;
            if (Q.president === Q.jxcat_neutral_candidate) Q.jxcat_neutral_available = false;
        }
        Q.jxcat_leader = "???";
        Q.jxcat_persuade_erc_available = Q.jxcat_erc_repeat_veto &&
            !(Q.jxcat_president_kind && Q.president === Q[cdc + "_leader"]) &&
            Q.jxcat_cdc_relations >= 55 && num(Q.erc_relations) >= 55 &&
            num(Q.party_resources) >= 1;
        Q.jxcat_failure_available = Q.player_party === "erc" || Q.jxcat_erc_repeat_veto ||
            !["cdc", "neutral", "erc", "president"].some(p => Q["jxcat_" + p + "_available"]);
    }
!}
go-to: choices_cup if player_party == "cup"; choices_erc if player_party == "erc"

# TODO: face-image

= A new proposal for National Unity

[? if jxsi_formed: In an attempt at continued National Unity,?][? if not jxsi_formed: In a new attempt at National Unity,?] the ANC is proposing a new unitary list: jxcat. Once again aiming at combining efforts for the sake of pursuing independence, it would hopefully bring together all pro-independence parties, including [+ parlament_current_ciu +], ERC, and even the CUP.

[? if jxsi_formed and not jxsi_dissolved: Basically, the question is if the current jxsi coalition is worth renewing. ?][? if jxsi_dissolved: While the breakup of jxsi still weighs on relations, there may be space for a new understanding. ?][? if not jxsi_formed: Where jxsi failed to prosper, its proponents seem bent on trying once again. ?][? if jxcat_president_available: Continuing under President [+ president +] would require no leadership negotiation resources, but other candidates remain possible. ?][? if jxcat_president_civic_veto: Civic organizations oppose continuing under President [+ president +] and demand a different candidate. ?][? if jxcat_erc_repeat_veto: ERC, however, is against yet another coalition led once more by [+ parlament_current_ciu +]. We may have a chance to persuade them, though... ?]

@choices_erc

- @erc_cdc
- @erc_neutral
- @erc_erc
- @erc_president
- @erc_refuse

@choices_cup

ERC and [+ parlament_current_ciu +] are negotiating who should lead the common list. We can let their agreement stand, or use our influence to bring them around to a different candidate. For now, we are deciding which agreement to support; whether the CUP itself joins will be a separate decision.

- @cup_cdc
- @cup_neutral
- @cup_erc
- @cup_president
- @persuade_erc
- @cup_refuse

@erc_cdc
title: Accept [+ jxcat_cdc_leader +] as leader
subtitle: The split will be 40-60 between ERC and [+ parlament_current_ciu +]
view-if: player_party == "erc" and (not jxcat_president_kind or president != jxcat_cdc_leader)
on-arrival: {!
    Q.jxcat_select_president = false;
    Q.jxcat_selected_leader = 'cdc';
!}
go-to: participation

