@persuade_erc
title: Persuade ERC to accept [+ jxcat_cdc_leader +]'s leadership
subtitle: Some significant bridge-building effort would be required on our end for them to mend their differences with [+ parlament_current_ciu +]. \[-1 resources\]
view-if: player_party == "cup" and jxcat_erc_repeat_veto and (not jxcat_president_kind or president != jxcat_cdc_leader)
choose-if: jxcat_persuade_erc_available
unavailable-subtitle: [? if erc_relations < 55: We don't have good enough relations with ERC. ?][? if jxcat_cdc_relations < 55: We don't have good enough relations with [+ parlament_current_ciu +]. ?][? if party_resources < 1: Not enough resources. ?]
on-arrival: {!
    if (!Q.jxcat_persuade_erc_available)
        throw new Error("ERC cannot be persuaded");
    Q.party_resources -= 1;
    Q.jxcat_persuade_erc_available = false;
    Q.jxcat_cdc_available = true;
    Q.jxcat_select_president = false;
    Q.jxcat_selected_leader = 'cdc';
!}
go-to: participation

@participation
title: Who will join the new list?
on-arrival: {!
    const leader = Q.jxcat_selected_leader;
    if (!(Q.jxcat_select_president ? Q.jxcat_president_available : Q["jxcat_" + leader + "_available"]))
        throw new Error("Unavailable JxCat leadership");
    Q.jxcat_failure_available = Q.player_party === "erc";
    Q.jxcat_leadership_cost = !Q.jxcat_select_president && leader !== "cdc" ? 1 : 0;
    Q.jxcat_formation_num = leader === "cdc" ? 40 : leader === "erc" ? 60 : 50;
    Q.jxcat_proposed_leader = Q.jxcat_select_president ? Q.president : leader === "neutral" ? Q.jxcat_neutral_candidate
        : Q[(leader === "cdc" ? Q.parlament_current_ciu : leader) + "_leader"];
    Q.jxcat_proposed_leader_gender = Q.jxcat_select_president ? Q.president_gender : leader === "neutral" ? "m"
        : Q[(leader === "cdc" ? Q.parlament_current_ciu : leader) + "_leader_gender"];
    Q.jxcat_cup_join_available = Q.player_party === "cup"
        ? Q.cup_poblelliure_strength > Q.cup_endavant_strength &&
            Q.rubicon &&
            Q.cup_poblelliure_dissent <= 20 && Q.cup_thirdsector_dissent <= 20 &&
            (leader !== "cdc" || (Q.erc_relations >= 55 && Q.jxcat_cdc_relations >= 55))
        : leader !== "cdc" && Q.cup_faction !== "Endavant" &&
            Q.cup_relations >= (Q.jxcat_selected_leader = 'neutral' ? 55 : 65) &&
            Q.rubicon &&
            Q.party_resources >= Q.jxcat_leadership_cost + 1;
    
!}
go-to: participation_cup if player_party == "cup"; participation_erc if player_party == "erc"

@participation_cup
title: Will the CUP join the agreement?
view-if: player_party == "cup"

ERC and [+ parlament_current_ciu +] seem to have come together accepted [+ jxcat_proposed_leader +]'s leadership. Now the decision comes back to us: will the CUP join in? 

- @cup_join_cup
- @cup_without_cup

@cup_join_cup
title: The CUP will join the list!
subtitle: [? if cup_in_jxsi: The jxsi formula will be repeated once more. ?][? if not cup_in_jxsi: This may be the time for true and wide National Unity after all. ?]
view-if: player_party == "cup"
choose-if: jxcat_cup_join_available
unavailable-subtitle: [? if cup_poblelliure_strength <= cup_endavant_strength: Poble Lliure is not strong enough within the party to overcome Endavant's opposition to joining. ?][? if cup_poblelliure_dissent > 20: Even within Poble Lliure, dissent with the party line is just too strong. ?][? if cup_thirdsector_dissent > 20: The Third Sector is too dissatisfied to support joining the common list. ?][? if jxcat_selected_leader == "cdc" and erc_relations < 55: We don't have enough mutual trust with ERC to enter a list led by [+ parlament_current_ciu +] alongside them. ?][? if jxcat_selected_leader == "cdc" and jxcat_cdc_relations < 55: Our relations with [+ parlament_current_ciu +] are just too strained. ?][? if not rubicon: The party does not feel the situation is extreme enough to justify such an extraordinary agreement. ?]
on-arrival: {!
    Q.jxcat_include_cup = true;
!}
go-to: formed

@cup_without_cup
title: JxCat is no place for us!
subtitle: The place for the CUP is in the streets and running as a critical alternative party.
view-if: player_party == "cup"
on-arrival: {!
    Q.jxcat_include_cup = false;
!}
go-to: formed

@cup_refuse
title: [? if jxcat_erc_repeat_veto: ERC refuses to be in the shadows of [+ parlament_current_ciu +] for a second time. ?][? if not jxcat_erc_repeat_veto: No agreement is reached! ?]
subtitle: [+ parlament_current_ciu +] will go ahead with jxcat alone. [? if jxsi_formed and not jxsi_dissolved: This will, of course, also mean the dissolution of jxsi.?]
view-if: player_party == "cup" and jxcat_failure_available
choose-if: jxcat_failure_available
go-to: refuse

@participation_erc
title: Who will join the new list?
view-if: player_party == "erc"

With a solid agreement between [+ parlament_current_ciu +] and ERC, the question becomes[? if jxsi_formed: , once again,?] if the CUP will join in this time or not. As usual, the internal dynamics of the CUP makes this a very complex process, and who's to know what the outcome of their assemblies will be.

- @erc_join_cup
- @erc_without_cup
- @erc_refuse

@erc_join_cup
title: Persuade CUP to join the list
subtitle: This will require quite the effort on our end. \[-1 resources\]
view-if: player_party == "erc"
choose-if: jxcat_cup_join_available
unavailable-subtitle: [? if jxcat_selected_leader == "cdc": CUP will not accept CDC leadership. ?][? if cup_faction == "Endavant": With an Endavant leadership, there is no way the CUP can join in such a list. ?][? if (jxcat_selected_leader != 'neutral' and cup_relations < 65) or (jxcat_selected_leader = 'neutral' and cup_relations < 55): Relations with CUP are not good enough. ?][? if not rubicon: The CUP does not feel the situation is extreme enough to justify such an extraordinary agreement. ?][? if party_resources < jxcat_leadership_cost + 1: Not enough resources. ?]
on-arrival: {!
    Q.jxcat_include_cup = true;
!}
go-to: formed

